Below is a practical architecture plus a working skeleton for a **fully reactive** Spring Boot app that consumes from many Kafka topics, extracts `nationalCode` from heterogeneous payloads, checks Redis, and triggers a business API — designed so adding a new topic/business is just adding one class.

---

## 1. Stack (all non-blocking)

| Concern | Choice | Why |
|---|---|---|
| Runtime | Spring Boot + **WebFlux** (Netty) | No servlet thread-per-request |
| Kafka | **reactor-kafka** (`KafkaReceiver`) | Backpressure, manual ack, partition-ordered processing. (`@KafkaListener` is blocking – avoid) |
| Redis | **Spring Data Redis Reactive** (Lettuce) | `ReactiveStringRedisTemplate` |
| Outbound HTTP | **WebClient** | Reactive HTTP client |
| Resilience | **Resilience4j** reactor operators | Retry, circuit breaker, timeouts, bulkhead |
| Observability | Micrometer + Actuator | Metrics, health, tracing |

