## 2. Core design: one generic pipeline + pluggable per-topic handlers

```
Kafka (topics A,B,C…) ──► KafkaReceiver ──► route by topic ──► TopicHandler<T>
                                                                  ├─ deserialize(T)
                                                                  ├─ extractNationalCode(T)
                                          Redis EXISTS ◄──────────┤
                                                                  ├─ onMatch(T)  ──► WebClient ► API
                                                                  └─ onNoMatch(T)
                                          ack offset / DLT on failure
```

The **pipeline is written once**; the only thing that varies per business is a `TopicHandler` implementation.

### 2.1 The extension point (SPI)

```java
public interface TopicHandler<T> {

    /** Kafka topic this handler owns. */
    String topic();

    /** Payload type for deserialization. */
    Class<T> payloadType();

    /** Each topic has a different shape – the handler knows where the national code lives. */
    String extractNationalCode(T payload);

    /** Business action when nationalCode exists in Redis (e.g. call an API). */
    Mono<Void> onMatch(T payload, String nationalCode);

    /** Optional hook when it does not exist. Default: do nothing. */
    default Mono<Void> onNoMatch(T payload, String nationalCode) {
        return Mono.empty();
    }
}
```

### 2.2 Handler registry (auto-discovers all handlers)

```java
@Component
public class TopicHandlerRegistry {

    private final Map<String, TopicHandler<?>> handlers;

    public TopicHandlerRegistry(List<TopicHandler<?>> discovered) {
        this.handlers = discovered.stream()
            .collect(Collectors.toUnmodifiableMap(TopicHandler::topic, h -> h,
                (a, b) -> { throw new IllegalStateException("Duplicate handler for topic " + a.topic()); }));
    }

    @SuppressWarnings("unchecked")
    public <T> TopicHandler<T> forTopic(String topic) {
        var h = (TopicHandler<T>) handlers.get(topic);
        if (h == null) throw new IllegalStateException("No handler registered for topic " + topic);
        return h;
    }

    public Set<String> topics() { return handlers.keySet(); }
}
```

Adding a new business = **add one `@Component` implementing `TopicHandler`**; the app automatically subscribes to that topic.

