## 3. Reactive ports (Redis + API)

```java
public interface NationalCodeLookup {
    Mono<Boolean> exists(String nationalCode);
}

@Component
@RequiredArgsConstructor
public class RedisNationalCodeLookup implements NationalCodeLookup {

    private final ReactiveStringRedisTemplate redis;
    private final AppProperties props;

    @Override
    public Mono<Boolean> exists(String nationalCode) {
        // Use hasKey if each code is a key; use opsForSet().isMember(...) if stored in a SET
        return redis.hasKey(props.redis().keyPrefix() + nationalCode)
                .timeout(props.redis().timeout())
                .defaultIfEmpty(false);
    }
}
```

Generic API client with resilience baked in, so handlers stay thin:

```java
@Component
@RequiredArgsConstructor
public class ResilientApiClient {

    private final WebClient webClient;
    private final CircuitBreakerRegistry cbRegistry;
    private final RetryRegistry retryRegistry;

    public <B> Mono<Void> post(String name, String uri, B body) {
        return webClient.post().uri(uri)
                .bodyValue(body)
                .retrieve()
                .onStatus(HttpStatusCode::is4xxClientError,
                        r -> r.bodyToMono(String.class).map(NonRetryableException::new))
                .onStatus(HttpStatusCode::is5xxServerError,
                        r -> r.bodyToMono(String.class).map(RetryableException::new))
                .toBodilessEntity()
                .then()
                .transformDeferred(CircuitBreakerOperator.of(cbRegistry.circuitBreaker(name)))
                .transformDeferred(RetryOperator.of(retryRegistry.retry(name)));
    }
}
```

