## 8. Extending for future businesses

| Need | Change |
|---|---|
| New topic with new payload | Add one `TopicHandler<T>` `@Component` – nothing else |
| Different lookup (e.g. DB instead of Redis) | New `NationalCodeLookup` implementation |
| Multiple actions on match | Compose in `onMatch`: `Mono.when(apiA, apiB)` or `apiA.then(apiB)` |
| Message filtering/enrichment before lookup | Add a `default Mono<T> preProcess(T)` hook to the SPI |
| Handler needs its own consumer group/config | Give `TopicHandler` an optional `ConsumerOverrides` method and create one `KafkaReceiver` per group in the pipeline |
| Transactional exactly-once | Switch to `receiveExactlyOnce()` + `KafkaSender` transactions (only if the "API" can be replaced by a Kafka output) |

### Testing tips
- Use **Testcontainers** (Kafka + Redis) with `@SpringBootTest` and `StepVerifier`.
- Unit test each handler in isolation (they're plain classes returning `Mono`).
- Enable **BlockHound** in tests to guarantee nothing blocks on Netty/Reactor threads.

